   {
    "id": "h4_00042",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     55
    ],
    "text": "[A81][/A81]CHANGE HISTORY",
    "placeholders": {
     "A81": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_461_11\" id=\"tag_17_461_11\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00043",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     57,
     1
    ],
    "text": "First released in Issue 3. Included for alignment with the POSIX.1-1988 standard.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00044",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     59
    ],
    "text": "[A82][/A82]Issue 5",
    "placeholders": {
     "A82": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_461_12\" id=\"tag_17_461_12\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00045",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The DESCRIPTION is updated for alignment with the POSIX Threads Extension.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00046",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I83]pthread_sigmask[/I83]() function is added for alignment with the POSIX Threads Extension.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I83": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00047",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     63
    ],
    "text": "[A84][/A84]Issue 6",
    "placeholders": {
     "A84": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_461_13\" id=\"tag_17_461_13\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00048",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I85]pthread_sigmask[/I85]() function is marked as part of the Threads option.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I85": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00049",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The SYNOPSIS for [I86]sigprocmask[/I86]() is marked as a CX extension to note that the presence of this function in the [A87][I88]&lt;signal.h&gt;[/I88][/A87] header is an extension to the ISO&nbsp;C standard.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I86": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A87": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/signal.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I88": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00050",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The following changes are made for alignment with the ISO&nbsp;POSIX-1:1996 standard:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00051",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     7,
     1,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The DESCRIPTION is updated to explicitly state the functions which may generate the signal.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00052",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The normative text is updated to avoid use of the term &quot;must&quot; for application requirements.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00053",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     11
    ],
    "text": "The [B89]restrict[/B89] keyword is added to the [I90]pthread_sigmask[/I90]() and [I91]sigprocmask[/I91]() prototypes for alignment with the\nISO/IEC&nbsp;9899:1999 standard.",
    "placeholders": {
     "B89": {
      "open": "<b>",
      "close": "</b>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I90": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I91": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00054",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     13
    ],
    "text": "IEEE&nbsp;Std&nbsp;1003.1-2001/Cor&nbsp;2-2004, item XSH/TC2/D6/105 is applied, updating &quot;process' signal mask&quot; to &quot;thread's\nsignal mask&quot; in the DESCRIPTION and RATIONALE sections.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00055",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     15
    ],
    "text": "IEEE&nbsp;Std&nbsp;1003.1-2001/Cor&nbsp;2-2004, item XSH/TC2/D6/106 is applied, adding the example to the EXAMPLES section.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00056",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     67
    ],
    "text": "[A92][/A92]Issue 7",
    "placeholders": {
     "A92": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_461_14\" id=\"tag_17_461_14\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00057",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I93]pthread_sigmask[/I93]() function is moved from the Threads option to the Base.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I93": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00058",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     69,
     3
    ],
    "text": "POSIX.1-2008, Technical Corrigendum 1, XSH/TC1-2008/0467 [319] is applied.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00059",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     71
    ],
    "text": "[A94][/A94]Issue 8",
    "placeholders": {
     "A94": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_461_15\" id=\"tag_17_461_15\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00060",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1132 is applied, clarifying the [EINVAL] error.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00061",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1636 is applied, clarifying the exceptions to the equivalence of [I95]pthread_sigmask[/I95]() and\n[I96]sigprocmask[/I96]().",
    "placeholders": {
     "I95": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I96": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00062",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     73,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Austin Group Defect 1731 is applied, clarifying that although [I97]pthread_sigmask[/I97]() has to deliver at least one of any\npending unblocked signals that exist after it has changed the currently blocked set of signals, there is no requirement that the\ndelivered signal(s) include any that were unblocked by the change.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I97": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00063",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     79
    ],
    "text": "&nbsp;",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   }
  ]
 }
